  "gaps": [
    "The capture says only \"credits\" and never names the unit type (semester or quarter). Semester is assumed and needs confirmation.",
    "The elective block is printed as 16 credits. GEN 101 is listed as \"Entry Point Course ... (Elective)\" and counts toward electives, so the open elective line is recorded as 13 credits (16 - 3). This keeps the ledger at the printed total of 67 credits.",
    "Global Campus Foundations is printed as 33 credits. Nine listed Foundations courses (27 credits) plus ECO 204 (Social Scientist Perspective) and BUS 340 (Interdisciplinary Oral Communication) from the core make up the 33. These two core courses are recorded only under core to avoid double counting (\"6 credits from the core may also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements\").",
    "No specific elective courses are named for the 13 remaining elective credits.",
    "Residency: \"At least 18 credits earned toward the Associate of Arts degree must be completed at the University of Arizona Global Campus.\" No specific course is designated as institution-only, so no requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "The capture states \"Additional prerequisite courses may be required\" but does not identify them for this program, apart from ENG 122 requiring ENG 121 or equivalent.",
    "The capture states that courses may be substituted to satisfy specific Global Campus Foundations requirements, but it does not list the allowable substitutions.",
    "The GEN 104 and TEC 100 substitution rules in the capture apply to bachelor students or named bachelor programs. Their applicability to this associate program is not stated.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 is required. Other grade minimums for individual courses are not stated."
  ],
